 **Picks:** as Pocket. **Settings:** Stepover 3, Stepdown 5, Stock to leave
 0, Entry Helix radius 1.
 
+**Pass starts at** (Passes tab) sets where each level starts:
+
+- **Auto** cuts the rings from the middle of the area outward. This is
+  the order that 2D Offset always cut.
+- **Outside** starts at the outer edge of the area and works in. With an
+  Outside containment, the outer edge is the stock edge: the tool starts
+  outside the stock, cuts one stepover at a time and ends on the part
+  wall. Use it to stop full-width slots in the stock.
+- **Inside** starts at the part or island wall and works out.
+
 **Do not touch** (Geometry tab, **Boundaries**): pick faces or edge chains
 to protect from every cut, plunge, ramp, helix, keep-down and rapid link
 across the full tool assembly (flutes, shank and holder). **Clearance**

From 327cf6bba0b9f5f62ae0491adf928908507dfbac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:51:47 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(2d): Pass starts at Inside/Outside cuts level curves
 of the start side

The ring rank of #3353 sorted whole closed loops. After a band splits,
one piece loop has arcs on the stock side and on the part side, and
the part-side arcs cut a full slot (8.03 mm wide for an 8 mm tool on
the second read's 100 x 40 / radius 15 band).

Inside and Outside now plan level curves of the start side alone
(sided_rings.rs): the outer loop eroded (Outside) or the holes grown
(Inside) by j stepovers, clipped to the area as open pieces, ring by
ring, then the far wall ring last. A new pass leads in from a piece
already cut (sided_chain.rs), so its entry lands in cleared stock.
Open pieces stop 50 um short of the far wall, so the lattice never
puts a feed across the wall ring. A level that starts on a wall gets
a toolpath note (start_wall_note). Auto is byte-identical:
waterline_passes is back to the main text.

Pinned by pass_start_engagement (motion) and
offset_pass_start::fig8_outside_offset_never_slots_along_a_level.

Refs #1448
Fixes #3316

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
